{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/451563-inhabit-in-the-dark-ages","id":451563,"title":"Inhabit in the Dark Ages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-21T08:50:28-07:00","id":451563,"title":"Inhabit in the Dark Ages","content":"Hello guys,<br /> <br /> I have a very limited experience with Wraith, so I'm sorry if this is a silly question.<br /> <br /> How would Inhabit work during the Medieval times? As i read trough the description, it looks like it affects mostly machines, but the Artificers are one of (or the) oldest Guild. How would Inhabit work in a time with no machines? Is there anything about it?<br /> <br /> Thank you,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5426-aecioborba","name":"aecioborba","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T10:26:33-07:00","id":451700,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing you're looking at the first or second edition core. According to Guildbook: Artificers, the Guild formed around soulforging; Inhabit was a useful outgrowth of that work.<br /> <br /> The preview of Wraith 20th Inhabit makes it less machine-focused. Inhabit's ancient arts there focus on soulforging: improving the Artificer's skill at soulforging, improving their ability to soak damage, and communing with soulforged objects. (Another ancient art derives from soulforging, allowing an Artificer to channel their Arcanoi through an object they're touching, and minimising the damage they take from that object.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T14:55:42-07:00","id":452033,"title":"","content":"What you're looking for is the precursor to Inhabit, called Kinesis. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kinesis\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a little more information</a>.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T23:56:58-07:00","id":452328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/451563-inhabit-in-the-dark-ages?p=452033#post452033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're looking for is the precursor to Inhabit, called Kinesis. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kinesis\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a little more information</a>.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't agree. Kinesis is primarily machine-focused (and geared for the early 20th century, not the medieval period). My fanon is that pre-industrial Inhabit Arts targeting Skinlands objects have basically long fallen out of favour (or got picked up by the Alchemists).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T00:36:38-07:00","id":452361,"title":"","content":"They did <i>have</i> machines in the Dark Ages and before, they just weren't powered. Artificers would have been able to do all kinds of useful (or terrible) things. Cause wheels to catch on the axle, hinges to catch, locks to refuse to open, pop doors open... They simply dealt with simple machines as opposed to complex ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T09:58:44-07:00","id":452785,"title":"","content":"I wonder how far can you take that?<br /> <br /> Could Inhabit/Kinesis cause a hammer to fly out of your hand when you try to pound in a nail? Something to bounce up an inclined plane? A screw to twist itself out no matter how hard your try to force it in? A lever to bend or break or send the user, not the object, flying up into the air? Etc.<br /> <br /> Somehow, some of those seem more like Outrage....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T10:58:39-07:00","id":452850,"title":"","content":"Maybe they used to be the same thing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T15:25:36-07:00","id":453252,"title":"","content":"Only problem is that Outrage is external to the object affected while Kinesis and Inhabit are internal. You can't get the possessed hammer with Outrage. More like a hammer than flies around the room hitting. Doesn't really matter to the things the hammer hits, but it does to the one doing the hitting. And the hammer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T16:15:34-07:00","id":460469,"title":"","content":"You could have some tempered Arcanoi with Outrage and Kinesis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}